{
  "id": "al6",
  "title": "Memory",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al6-l1",
      "title": "Addresses",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Memory is a row of 256 bytes, numbered from 000 to 377 (octal). The number is the byte's address. Your program starts at address 000.",
        "LDA (072) loads a byte from memory into A. It needs the address in the next two bytes: the low byte first, then the high byte (always 000 on our small Altair).",
        "Data can sit right after HLT: count the bytes of the program to find its address."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "072   ; 000: LDA",
          "006   ;      address 006 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 003: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 005: HLT",
          "143   ; 006: the data"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○●●○○○●● = 99"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al6-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "At which address does the program start?",
          "options": [
            "000",
            "001",
            "377",
            "100"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The first byte you deposit goes to address 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "al6-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many bytes does LDA take in the program?",
          "options": [
            "3: the opcode and a two-byte address",
            "1",
            "2",
            "4"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "072, the low byte, the high byte."
        },
        {
          "id": "al6-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why is the data at address 006?",
          "options": [
            "The program before it takes 6 bytes (000 to 005)",
            "LDA always uses 006",
            "It's random",
            "HLT is at 006"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "LDA (3 bytes) + OUT (2) + HLT (1) = 6."
        },
        {
          "id": "al6-l1-e4",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to LDA (0 7 2).",
          "answer": 58,
          "explanation": "00 111 010."
        },
        {
