          ],
          "options": [
            "25",
            "6",
            "0",
            "an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "LDA 006 loads the byte at address 006, which is 25."
        },
        {
          "id": "al6-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which byte of the address comes first?",
          "options": [
            "The low byte",
            "The high byte",
            "It doesn't matter",
            "Only one byte is used"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The 8080 is little-endian: low byte first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al6-l2",
      "title": "STA and LDA",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "STA (062) stores A at an address. LDA brings it back. With them, a program can remember results in memory.",
        "Free memory after your program is the place for results. In these lessons, address 200 (octal) is used as a scratch byte.",
        "A program can even change its own bytes in memory. Early programmers did that, but it makes programs very hard to read."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "115   ;      77",
          "062   ; 002: STA",
          "200   ;      address 200 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "076   ; 005: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "072   ; 007: LDA",
          "200   ;      address 200 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 014: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○●○○●●○● = 77"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al6-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does STA 200 do?",
          "options": [
            "Stores A at address 200",
            "Loads address 200 into A",
            "Shows address 200",
            "Jumps to 200"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "STore A."
        },
        {
          "id": "al6-l2-e2",
          "type": "switches",
