    {
      "id": "al6-l3",
      "title": "HL and M",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Registers H and L together hold a whole address: LXI H (041) puts one into them, low byte first. Then M means \"the memory byte at address HL\".",
        "MOV A,M (176) reads that byte, MOV M,A (167) writes it, ADD M (206) adds it. INX H (043) moves HL on to the next byte.",
        "That's how programs walk through tables of data, one byte after the other."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "041   ; 000: LXI H data",
          "013   ;      address 013 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "176   ; 003: MOV A,M",
          "043   ; 004: INX H",
          "206   ; 005: ADD M",
          "043   ; 006: INX H",
          "206   ; 007: ADD M",
          "323   ; 010: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 012: HLT",
          "012   ; 013: data: 10",
          "024   ; 014: data: 20",
          "014   ; 015: data: 12"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○●○●○●○ = 42"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
